# .silent-exit-allowlist (T-2666) — confirmed-loud non-zero process::exit sites.
#
# scripts/check-silent-exit.sh flags a `std::process::exit(<non-zero int literal>)` whose
# immediately-preceding statement is a lone `}` closing a `json_error_exit`-bearing block,
# with no output macro between the brace and the exit (the T-2663 json-gated / bare-text-exit
# class). A site here is acknowledged as actually-loud (it emits user-facing output through a
# path the line-window cannot see).
#
# Format: one drift-stable signature per line —
#   <relpath>::<enclosing-fn>::silent-exit
# fn-name-based, so it survives line moves; a fn RENAME re-fires the site (intended re-review).
# `#` starts a comment; blank lines are ignored.
#
# The current tree scans CLEAN after the T-2667 sibling migration (session.rs cmd_list,
# remote.rs cmd_remote_list_inner both now emit an actionable stderr line before the bare
# exit, mirroring the T-2663 remediation at metadata.rs), so this allowlist is empty.
